---
description: Cross-repository P2PFlow MVP identity, technology, verification, and constraints.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

# project.mdc

```yaml
project:
  name: p2pflow-base-sepolia-mvp
  displayName: P2PFlow Base Sepolia MVP
  type: microservice

repositories:
  primary: p2pflow/p2pflow-smart-contract
  modifiable:
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-smart-contract
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-subgraph
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-user-ui
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-merchant-ui
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-admin-ui
    - local/p2pflow-executor
  readOnly:
    - p2pdotme/user-app-client
    - p2pdotme/p2pdotme-sdk
    - p2pdotme/executor
    - p2pdotme/subgraph
  involved:
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-smart-contract
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-subgraph
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-user-ui
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-merchant-ui
    - p2pflow/p2pflow-admin-ui
    - local/p2pflow-executor
  localWorkspace: true

technology:
  languages:
    - Solidity
    - JavaScript
    - JSX
    - TypeScript
    - AssemblyScript
    - GraphQL
  languageVersions:
    Solidity: 0.8.24
    Node.js: 24.x LTS target
    ECMAScript: ES2022
  frameworks:
    - Hardhat 2
    - OpenZeppelin Contracts 5
    - EIP-2535 Diamond
    - React 18/19
    - Vite 5
    - Thirdweb v5
    - TanStack Query 5
    - The Graph / Goldsky
    - planned Fastify modular executor
  buildTool: npm with Hardhat, Vite, and Graph CLI
  testCommands:
    fullSuite: npm test
    singleClass: npx hardhat test test/orders.test.js
  packageRoots:
    - contracts
    - scripts
    - test
    - ../p2pflow-subgraph/src
    - ../p2pflow-user-ui/src
    - ../p2pflow-merchant-ui/src
    - ../p2pflow-admin-ui/src
    - ../p2pflow-executor/src
  routeConfigPatterns:
    - ../p2pflow-user-ui/src/App.jsx
    - ../p2pflow-merchant-ui/src/App.jsx
    - ../p2pflow-admin-ui/src/App.jsx
    - ../p2pflow-executor/src/http/**/*.ts

bugbot:
  enabled: false
  repoUrl: https://github.com/p2pflow/p2pflow-smart-contract
  triggerOnDraftPr: false
  triggerComment: /bugbot
  botLogins: []
  setupDoc: .cursor/docs/bugbot-setup.md

jira:
  enabled: false
  baseUrl: TBD
  projectKey: TBD
  projectStyle: team-managed
  issueTypes:
    epic: Epic
    story: Story
    task: Task
    subtask: Sub-task

branching:
  defaultBranch: dev
  workingBranch: codex-2
  mergeStrategy: merge
  commitConvention: conventional

dependencies:
  internal:
    - shared generated Diamond ABI and deployment manifest
    - executor HTTP/session API
    - Goldsky subgraph read model
  external:
    - Base Sepolia chain 84532
    - Circle Base Sepolia USDC
    - Alchemy RPC
    - Thirdweb wallet SDK
    - Goldsky hosted subgraph
    - PostgreSQL
    - multiple price data providers

agentVerification:
  runLocally: true
  ciCommands:
    compile: npm run compile
    unitTests: npm test
    contractSecurity: npm test
    subgraph: npm run codegen && npm run build
    ui: npm run lint && npm run build
    executor: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build
  skipLocal: []
  deferTo:
    - coordinated GitHub pull-request checks when repository remotes are available
    - pre-PR dependency reconciliation and minimum compilation

constraints:
  - Base Sepolia only for this phase; never deploy or configure mainnet
  - Use codex-2 from latest origin/dev in all existing P2PFlow repositories, overriding generic branch naming
  - Build one deployable modular executor; do not create separate pricing, matching, auth, or scanner microservices
  - Do not commit secrets, tokens, private keys, or .env files
  - Never use the exposed workspace deployer key for signing or deployment
  - Keep all VITE variables public-only; Thirdweb secret and Goldsky token are server-only
  - Do not modify p2pme reference repositories
  - Do not edit .cursor kit files outside .cursor/project-context; workflow state/reports are local and gitignored
  - Contract custody and eligibility checks remain authoritative; subgraph data is never a security authority
```
